; Four collapses, for two reasons.
;
; `:value` reaches nothing — a string is neither the number arm nor the
; vector arm — so there is no arm to report. `:both`, `:size` and `:shape`
; each reach two, so reporting one would be a guess about which the author
; meant. `:shape` is the sharp case: the two form kinds accept disjoint
; HEADS, which looks like disjointness but is a refinement, and deciding it
; would mean running the match. Reachability stops at the node shape.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code union_no_branch_matched :path [k value])
  (diagnostic :code union_no_branch_matched :path [k both])
  (diagnostic :code union_no_branch_matched :path [k size])
  (diagnostic :code union_no_branch_matched :path [k shape]))
